    "title": "How many workers?",
    "body": "A worker does one job at a time. Building an invoice takes 0.8 seconds, so one worker finishes 1 ÷ 0.8 = 1.25 invoices per second. At a sale, 50 orders arrive per second: 50 ÷ 1.25 = **40 workers** busy all the time, or 50 × 0.8 = 40 in one step. To keep them at most 70% busy, run 40 ÷ 0.7 ≈ 57.",
