  {
    "title": "The backlog grows",
    "body": "With only 30 workers, capacity is 30 × 1.25 = 37.5 invoices per second. At 50 per second, the **backlog** grows by 50 − 37.5 = 12.5 per second: after a 10-minute sale, 12.5 × 600 = **7,500** invoices are waiting. The order page is still fast, because the queue absorbs the difference. When orders fall to 10 per second, the backlog drains at 37.5 − 10 = 27.5 per second: 7,500 ÷ 27.5 ≈ 273 seconds, about 4.5 minutes.",
