  {
    "title": "A crash before the ack",
    "body": "A worker takes the message for order 123 and the broker hides it from other workers for 30 seconds (the **visibility timeout**). The worker sends the email, then crashes before its **acknowledgment**. No ack arrives, so after 30 seconds the broker gives the message to another worker, which sends the email again. This is **at-least-once delivery**: nothing is lost, but work can repeat. Acknowledging before sending would be worse: a crash would lose the email.",
