  {
    "title": "Make repeats harmless",
    "body": "The fix is an **idempotency key**. The worker sends the order id with the email request, and the email provider ignores a second request with the same key, so the customer gets one email however often the message repeats. Inside your own database, a unique constraint does the same job (SD 4): a second insert of \"email sent for order 123\" fails. With at-least-once delivery, every consumer must make its work safe to repeat.",
