  {
    "title": "One event, many listeners",
    "body": "In **publish-subscribe**, the app publishes \"order placed\" once, and each subscriber gets its own copy in its own queue: email, invoice and warehouse each have their own workers, so a down warehouse does not delay emails. An **event log**, such as Kafka, also keeps every message for a set time, such as 7 days; each consumer tracks its own position, its **offset**, and can read the history again. If a backlog passes its limit, the producer applies **back-pressure**: it slows down, refuses new work, or skips optional work such as marketing emails.",
